      <statement><p>Determine which of the following statements are true and which are false.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p>If <m>\displaystyle A</m> and <m>\displaystyle B</m> are square matrices of the same size then <m>\displaystyle (A+B)^2 = A^2 + 2AB + B^2</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The matrices <m>\displaystyle A^TA</m> and <m>\displaystyle AA^T</m> are always square, regardless of the size of <m>\displaystyle A</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If <m>\displaystyle A \in \mathcal{M}_{n,m}</m> and <m>\displaystyle \mathbf{b} \in \mathbb{R}^m</m> is a column vector, then <m>\displaystyle A\mathbf{b}</m> is a linear combination of the columns of <m>\displaystyle A</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If <m>\displaystyle A \in \mathcal{M}_{n,m}</m> and <m>\displaystyle \mathbf{b} \in \mathbb{R}^m</m> is a column vector, then <m>\displaystyle A\mathbf{b}</m> is a linear combination of the rows of <m>\displaystyle A</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>If <m>\displaystyle A</m> and <m>\displaystyle B</m> are square matrices of the same size, then <m>\displaystyle (AB)^T = A^TB^T</m>.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
