      <statement><p>For what values of <m>c</m> will
<m>\displaystyle A = \begin{bmatrix} 1 \amp  1 \\ c \amp  c^2 \end{bmatrix}</m> be invertible?</p>
<p>For all <m>c</m> such that <m>c\neq</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/> and <m>c\neq</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0002"/>.</p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>0</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>1</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <solution><p><alert>SOLUTION:</alert> 
The matrix <m>\displaystyle A = \begin{bmatrix} 1 \amp  1 \\ c \amp  c^2 \end{bmatrix}</m> is invertible provided the columns of <m>A</m> are linearly independent, which will be the case if <m>c \neq c^2</m>. Thus, we require that <m>c\neq 0</m> and <m>c \neq 1</m>.</p>
</solution>
